{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1791477558-5GsvYIz6pvkfXQCZf23j","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the payments key to diagnose the 401 errors.\n\nThe key in .env is a Stripe publishable key (pk_live_). Server-side payment API calls require a secret key (sk_live_). The current test also incorrectly validates for the wrong prefix.\n\nThe key appears truncated. Standard Stripe keys are typically over 100 characters, but this one is much shorter.\n\nThe key is only 56 characters long. A valid Stripe publishable key should be significantly longer.\n\nThe actual payment API code is not in this repository. Only config loading and tests reference the key.\n\nI will keep the diagnosis brief and avoid echoing any secrets.","signature":""}],"model":"x-ai/grok-4.7","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"xAI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6afedc5-bb4d-48f7-b3d5-618d040544e4","uuid":"3a464f24-90b6-4267-bf66-b013fc00324e","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:39:33.309Z","request_id":"gen-1791477558-5GsvYIz6pvkfXQCZf23j","thinking_duration_ms":11115}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1791477558-5GsvYIz6pvkfXQCZf23j","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The payments key is the wrong kind for server-side calls, which is why those requests are coming back 401.\n\n`.env` sets `PAYMENTS_KEY` to a Stripe **publishable** key (`pk_live_…`). Publishable keys are meant for the browser. Secret API calls (PaymentIntents, charges, refunds) need a **secret** key (`sk_live_…`) or a restricted key (`rk_live_…`). Stripe rejects a `pk_` key on those endpoints with 401.\n\nThe check in `test.js` only asserts that the value starts with `pk_`, so `npm test` will print `ok` even though this key cannot authenticate payment calls.\n\nSwap in the live secret key from the Stripe dashboard (Developers → API keys) and restart the process that reads `.env`. Do not put the secret key in client code. The value in `.env` is also shorter than current Stripe live keys, so if the secret you paste still 401s, confirm it was copied in full.","citations":[]}],"model":"x-ai/grok-4.7","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"xAI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6afedc5-bb4d-48f7-b3d5-618d040544e4","uuid":"7d265604-354a-46e9-b4fd-cee5de4e2824","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:39:35.268Z","request_id":"gen-1791477558-5GsvYIz6pvkfXQCZf23j"}
